Chapter: ProbeClosureBaseShow

 Isolator for tier 14's missing control. `even-fn 0` takes the branch
 that returns `add3 5` with no recursion at all, and the three arguments
 arrive exactly as they do in the recursive case.

 It FAULTS. probe-closure-rec-cmp, the same chapter with `even-fn 4`
 four levels deeper, answers instead. The base case being the fatal one
 is why tier 14's control is `pick` rather than this, and it is the
 sharp form of the recursion oddity finding 39 records as unexplained:
 recursion is not merely load-bearing for the silent case, its absence
 here is fatal.

 Pairs with probe-closure-basecase, which found the same inversion in
 the count-down shape and retired PR 78's framing.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  even-fn : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  even-fn (n) = if n == 0 then add3 5 else odd-fn (n - 1)

  odd-fn : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  odd-fn (n) = even-fn n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("base-show " & show (((even-fn 0) 20) 22))
  end
